---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TalkBanner from '../components/TalkBanner.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../config/paths';
---

<BaseLayout page="privacy">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <LegalDoc
    title="Privacy notice"
    updated="27 October 2026"
    note="Draft: this notice has not been reviewed by a solicitor yet. It describes the site as it works today and will be updated before we collect any personal data beyond a direct enquiry."
  >
    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      This notice covers this website, run by {site.founder} trading as {site.name} (a working name
      — see the footer for current contact details). Gurman has not yet registered as a sole trader;
      that is planned before any paid work begins.
    </p>

    <h2>This site itself</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts of any kind.
      It is a static set of pages: visiting it does not create an account, a session or a tracking
      profile. If analytics are added later, this notice will be updated first and a cookie or
      consent notice will be added if required.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted by Cloudflare, which briefly processes standard request details (your IP
      address, browser type and the page asked for) to deliver the page and protect the site from
      abuse. We don't use those logs to track or profile anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>If you use a form</h2>
    <p>
      The contact form and the free AI check form ask for your name, an email to reply to, and
      optionally your website, phone number and a message. When you press send, those details are
      passed through Cloudflare and emailed straight to our inbox (Gmail, run by Google). They are
      not saved on the website or in any database, and we use them only to answer you. The enquiry
      email is kept only as long as needed to answer you and, if you become a client, as part of the
      project record. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in replying to an enquiry you
      started.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you give a website address, we load that site's public home page, robots.txt and llms.txt
      once, automatically, and add a short summary to the email (its title, how quickly it answered
      and whether it lets AI crawlers in). That is information about the website, not about you.
    </p>
    <p>The forms include a hidden field that catches spam bots; it collects nothing about you.</p>

    <h2>If you call, email or message us directly</h2>
    <p>
      The email address and phone number open your own email app or dialler. That message goes
      directly from your device to us, the same as if you'd looked up the details yourself, and is
      handled like any other enquiry.
    </p>

    <h2>If you become a client</h2>
    <p>
      Any project involving an AI assistant, booking system or similar tool will have its own,
      specific explanation of what data is collected, which providers process it, and how long it is
      kept, agreed with you before launch. Health-related businesses (for example dental or
      physiotherapy clients) get extra care here, in line with the rules for special-category data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what information is held about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or
      raise a concern, by contacting{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. If you're not satisfied
      with the response, you can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies. The <a href={withBase('/cookies/')}>cookie policy</a> has the
      details.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>

  <TalkBanner />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
